hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"174","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about ablution. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed three ablutions. Thirdly, he said: “Whoever does more has done wrong and is unjust, or has transgressed and done injustice.”"
